# promscope tool requests - needs a running Prometheus and promscope:
#   docker run -d --rm --name prom -p 9090:9090 prom/prometheus
#   go run ./cmd/promscope
#
# Prometheus scrapes itself out of the box, so prometheus_* and go_* metrics
# exist within seconds of starting - real data, no exporters needed yet.

### 1. tools/list - the tool catalog: check name, description, annotations,
### input schema (filter) and output schema (metrics/total/truncated/hint)
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "method": "tools/list"}

### 2. list_metrics, no filter - expect a few hundred names, enriched
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "list_metrics", "arguments": {}}}

### 3. list_metrics with filter - only go_* runtime metrics
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "list_metrics", "arguments": {"filter": "go_gc"}}}

### 4. filter with no matches - expect total 0 and a "broader filter" hint
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 13, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "list_metrics", "arguments": {"filter": "vllm"}}}

### 5. invalid input - filter must be a string; the SDK's schema validation
### rejects this before our handler ever runs
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "list_metrics", "arguments": {"filter": 42}}}

### 6. Prometheus down (docker stop prom, then run this) - expect isError:true
### with an actionable message, NOT a protocol error
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "list_metrics", "arguments": {}}}

### 7. get_alerts - a vanilla `docker run` Prometheus has no alert rules, so
### expect total 0 with the "no alert rules configured" hint (the compose
### demo stack DOES ship an always-firing rule, so expect AlwaysFiring there)
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "get_alerts", "arguments": {}}}

### 8. get_alerts with an invalid state - expect isError naming valid values
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 17, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "get_alerts", "arguments": {"state": "resolved"}}}

### 9. query_metrics instant - aggregated, so it stays under the series cap
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 20, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "query_metrics", "arguments": {"query": "sum by (handler) (rate(prometheus_http_requests_total[5m]))"}}}

### 10. query_metrics range - relative start, auto-computed step (watch stepUsed)
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 21, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "query_metrics", "arguments": {"query": "go_goroutines", "mode": "range", "start": "-15m"}}}

### 11. step coarsening - 1s over 10h would be 36000 points; expect stepUsed 3m1s
### (ceil(36000s / 199) - the divisor is maxPoints-1, see chooseStep) and a
### "coarsened" hint
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 22, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "query_metrics", "arguments": {"query": "go_goroutines", "mode": "range", "start": "-10h", "step": "1s"}}}

### 12. lookback guardrail - 25h window, expect isError naming the 24h limit
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 23, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "query_metrics", "arguments": {"query": "up", "mode": "range", "start": "-25h"}}}

### 13. resources/list - the one resource, prometheus://rules
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 40, "method": "resources/list"}

### 14. resources/read - against a vanilla Prometheus expect empty groups
### plus the explanatory note; against the compose stack expect both rule kinds
POST http://localhost:8090/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 41, "method": "resources/read", "params": {"uri": "prometheus://rules"}}
